Added `AIProvider.provider_type`, which records which API dialect an endpoint speaks: OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenAI-compatible, or Ollama. `openai_compatible` keeps its meaning and answers a different question: whether models can be discovered at the endpoint. A consuming app reads the dialect to decide how to address the provider, which the boolean cannot tell it. Ollama is the case that makes the two distinct, because its OpenAI-compatibility layer serves `GET /v1/models` but does not return tool calls in the `tool_calls` field.
Added validation refusing an OpenAI-compatible or Ollama provider whose External Integration carries no remote URL. Those two types are an address rather than a service, and a client with no URL for one of them falls back to a default endpoint that belongs to somebody else.
Added a data migration that fills `provider_type` in from `openai_compatible`. A provider that served the OpenAI shape becomes `openai_compatible`. A provider that did not is left blank, because the boolean says nothing about what such an endpoint speaks instead, and an operator is asked to answer the next time the row is saved.
